  [1mWhat removing [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m from [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m actually does[0m ([38;5;153mserver.js:7[39m): it makes the only authenticated endpoint
  in this service fully public. There is no network boundary in this code — [38;5;153mapp.listen[39m binds all interfaces, and the
  route returns revenue data ([38;5;153m{ quarter: "Q1", revenue: 42 }[39m). Anyone who can reach the port gets it, not just the
  dashboard script. "Internal" is a property of the deployment, not of this file, and I can't confirm it from here. Note
  also that [38;5;153m/reports/public[39m already exists unauthenticated, so the split between the two routes is deliberate.

  It is one line, but the line is the access control.

