     gets a credential; the route stays closed. ~5 lines in [38;5;153mauth.js[39m.
  2. [1mServe the data from [38;5;153m/reports/public[0m — if the dashboard only needs the rows and they aren't sensitive, expose that
     specific payload on the already-public route instead of unlocking the admin one.
  3. [1mRemove the check as asked[0m — if you can confirm the service is genuinely unreachable from outside and that's an
     accepted risk.

